    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d734">

                <pb facs="0649" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/18379</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Garrett to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laredo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-11T15:00:00-06:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 11, 1916, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mexicans raided Texas forty five miles above Laredo last night and took eighty
                    horses from a Texas ranch. General Ozuna has been sent to Lampazos with his full
                    command, styled a brigade. The bandits who raided Texas are a part of the de la
                    Rosa outfit.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
